From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: windows.applicationmodel: implement ResourceLoader over a PRI reader

Applications localised with MRT keep their strings in a Package Resource Index
(resources.pri) and read them through
Windows.ApplicationModel.Resources.ResourceLoader. Wine had neither the class
nor a PRI reader, so RoGetActivationFactory failed and such programs showed
resource keys instead of text: winget printed "ToolDescription",
"InstallCommandShortDescription", column headers as key names, and so on.

Add a bounds-checked reader for the PRI format (mrm_pri0-3/prif: the
descriptor, hierarchical schema, decision info, resource map and data item
sections), written from the format as documented by independent open-source
readers, and the ResourceLoader runtime class on top of it: activation
(the "Resources" map), IResourceLoaderFactory, IResourceLoaderStatics(2,4),
GetString and GetStringForUri. The index is the executable directory's
resources.pri (the package root of an unpacked package), else <exe>.pri.
Candidates are chosen by the user's preferred UI languages, falling back to
the index's default language; a missing resource is an empty string, as on
Windows.

Tested by test/resources-gate.sh against a generated index (test/mkpri.py)
and against winget's own resources.pri; the parser was fuzzed with 20000
mutated indexes under AddressSanitizer.

